  _landmarkId: fuji-dagi
  _displayTitle: Mount Fuji
  _shortDescription: At 3,776 metres, Mount Fuji is Japan's highest mountain and
    a stratovolcano still considered active. Its nearly perfect cone has inspired
    artists, pilgrims, and travellers for centuries. The sacred mountain last erupted
    in 1707 and became an enduring symbol in art beyond Japan through Hokusai's celebrated
    prints.
  _sector: JAPAN
  _displayTitleTurkish: "Fuji Da\u011F\u0131"
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "3.776 metre y\xFCksekli\u011Findeki Fuji, Japonya\u2019n\u0131n
    en y\xFCksek da\u011F\u0131 ve h\xE2l\xE2 aktif kabul edilen bir stratovolkand\u0131r.
    Neredeyse kusursuz konisi y\xFCzy\u0131llard\u0131r sanat\xE7\u0131lara, hac\u0131lara
    ve gezginlere ilham verir. Son b\xFCy\xFCk patlamas\u0131 1707\u2019de ger\xE7ekle\u015Fen
    kutsal da\u011F, Hokusai\u2019nin \xFCnl\xFC bask\u0131lar\u0131 sayesinde Japonya
    d\u0131\u015F\u0131ndaki sanat d\xFCnyas\u0131nda da kal\u0131c\u0131 bir simgeye
    d\xF6n\xFC\u015Ft\xFC."
  _sectorTurkish: JAPONYA
